graph" class=3D"description KbDetailLtContainer__description" tabindex=3D"-=
1"><h3 id=3D"heading-d25fa9c6-dd00-b8f7" tabindex=3D"0">Overview</h3>
<p>The Equation question type calculates a value from earlier answers and s=
aves it in the response =E2=80=94 a running score, a BMI, a random group nu=
mber, or a tailored sentence. It supports any syntax that <a href=3D"https:=
//www.limesurvey.org/manual/ExpressionScript_-_Presentation">ExpressionScri=
pt</a> understands.</p>
<p>Three things make it special:</p>
<ul>
<li><b>It computes even when hidden.</b> Unlike every other question type, =
a hidden equation is still evaluated and its value stored in the database =
=E2=80=94 which is exactly how it is usually used: as an invisible calculat=
or.</li>
<li><b>It can assign values to other questions</b> via the assignment opera=
tor.</li>
<li><b>No HTML is saved</b> in the database, for security reasons.</li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"heading-20497396-1137-1d97" tabindex=3D"0">Add and edit the quest=
ion</h3>
<ol>
<li>Click the <b>+</b> button and choose <b>Equation</b> from the <b>Number=
</b> group.</li>
<li>Put your expression, in curly brackets, into the question. The cleanest=
 way is the dedicated <b>Equation</b> setting in the question's settings pa=
nel =E2=80=94 that keeps the stored value separate from the display text (a=
nd works across languages). You can then show a friendly sentence in the qu=
estion text, such as "Your BMI is {self.NAOK}", while only the calculated v=
alue is saved.</li>
<li>If the result is a number, also enable the <b>Numbers only</b> advanced=
 setting, so the value is stored as a proper numeric variable for statistic=
s and exports.</li>
</ol>
<h3 id=3D"heading-e1e246ea-9b50-82ff" tabindex=3D"0">Common examples</h3>
<p>Assume earlier questions have the codes <code>weight</code>, <code>heigh=
t</code>, <code>q1</code>=E2=80=93<code>q3</code>. Give the equation questi=
on its own code (e.g. <code>score</code>) so you can reuse the result later=
.</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Total score:</b> <code>{sum(q1.NAOK, q2.NAOK, q3.NAOK)}</code> =E2=
=80=94 adds up the answers.</li>
<li><b>BMI:</b> <code>{weight / (height * height)}</code> =E2=80=94 the cla=
ssic calculation example (a ready-made sample survey is linked below).</li>
<li><b>Random group (A/B test):</b> <code>{rand(1, 2)}</code> =E2=80=94 ran=
domly stores 1 or 2. Hide the question, and each respondent is randomly ass=
igned to group 1 or group 2.</li>
<li><b>Category from a value:</b> <code>{if(score &gt; 10, 'High', 'Low')}<=
/code> =E2=80=94 stores "High" or "Low" depending on the score.</li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"heading-82b9ffd8-343d-d47b" tabindex=3D"0">Using the result for c=
onditions</h3>
<p>The stored value behaves like any other answer, which makes equations th=
e standard trick for branching logic:</p>
<ul>
<li>In the <b>Condition designer</b> ("New logic" in a later question's set=
tings), reference the equation's code =E2=80=94 for example, show a questio=
n group only when <code>rand1</code> equals <code>1</code>, or ask follow-u=
p questions only when <code>score &gt; 10</code>.</li>
<li>In later question <i>text</i>, pipe the value in with its code: <code>{=
score}</code>.</li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"heading-d815f635-b5dc-fa42" tabindex=3D"0">Related Resources</h3>
<p><a href=3D"https://manual.limesurvey.org/Special:Filepath/Limesurvey_sur=
vey_BMIsample.lss.zip">Download the sample survey</a> (Limesurvey_survey_BM=
Isample.lss.zip) to see a working BMI calculator built with this question t=
ype.</p>
<p>See also <a href=3D"https://help.limesurvey.org/portal/en/kb/articles/us=
e-answers-from-previous-questions-piping">Use answers from previous questio=
ns (piping)</a> for referencing codes in text, and <a href=3D"https://help.=
limesurvey.org/portal/en/kb/articles/mask-questions">Mask Questions</a> for=
 related question types.</p>
